# Tailwind className Standards

## Always use `cn` for className composition

Never concatenate or template-literal className strings directly. Always use the `cn` utility (from `@/lib/utils`) to combine classes, even for a single conditional. Do not comment each line, just group by concern.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className={`flex flex-col ${isActive ? "text-emerald-400" : "text-neutral-400"}`} />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className={cn("flex flex-col", isActive ? "text-emerald-400" : "text-neutral-400")} />
```

## Split long className strings across multiple lines

When a className string would exceed ~80 characters, split it into grouped logical chunks inside `cn`. Each string argument should represent one concern — do not mix concerns in a single string.

### Class ordering — group by concern, top to bottom

This mirrors the order enforced by `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss`:

| Order | Concern             | Examples                                                        |
| ----- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1     | **Layout**          | `flex`, `grid`, `block`, `relative`, `absolute`, `overflow-*`   |
| 2     | **Spacing**         | `p-*`, `px-*`, `py-*`, `m-*`, `gap-*`                           |
| 3     | **Sizing**          | `w-*`, `h-*`, `size-*`, `max-*`, `min-*`                        |
| 4     | **Typography**      | `text-{size}`, `font-*`, `leading-*`, `tracking-*`, `uppercase` |
| 5     | **Presentational**  | `bg-*`, `border-*`, `rounded-*`, `shadow-*`                     |
| 6     | **Colour**          | `text-{colour}`, `fill-*`, `stroke-*`                           |
| 7     | **Animation**       | `transition-*`, `duration-*`, `ease-*`, `animate-*`             |
| 8     | **State modifiers** | `hover:*`, `focus:*`, `active:*`, `disabled:*`, `dark:*`        |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — mixed concerns, unreadable at a glance
<a className="flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-1.5 border-t border-neutral-700/60 px-3 py-2.5 text-xs font-medium text-neutral-400 transition-colors hover:text-emerald-400" />

// ✅ GOOD — each line is one concern, ordered layout → state
<a
  className={cn(
    "flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-2.5", // layout + spacing
    "border-t border-neutral-700/60",                               // presentational
    "text-xs font-medium text-neutral-400",                         // typography + colour
    "transition-colors hover:text-emerald-400",                     // animation + state
  )}
/>
```

> **Tip:** Layout and spacing can share a line when tightly related (e.g. a flex row with its gap/padding). Presentational, colour, animation, and state should each be their own line.
